========================================================================
                    PORTABLE ED TEST CORPUS
========================================================================

cases.json is the stable version 1 collection of black-box ed tests.  It can be
used by implementations written in C, Rust, TypeScript, Go, or any other
language.  The corpus does not import tsed code and contains no material from
private conformance suites.

Each case has these fields:

    name        stable descriptive identifier
    arguments   command-line arguments passed to ed
    stdin       exact bytes supplied to standard input
    stdout      exact expected standard output
    stderr      exact expected standard error
    status      expected process exit status

All strings currently contain ASCII text encoded as UTF-8.  Cases use -s to
suppress byte counts and write the final buffer to /dev/null before quitting.
This keeps them deterministic while using only POSIX interfaces.

Run the corpus against tsed after building it:

    bun run test:portable

Run it against another implementation:

    bun test/portable_runner.ts /path/to/ed

or:

    TSED_TEST_ED=/path/to/ed bun run test:portable

The JSON file is the public interface.  The supplied runner uses Bun only for
convenience; another project may consume the same file with any JSON parser and
process-launching API.

Version 2
------------------------------------------------------------------------

cases-v2.json adds the process behavior needed by the POSIX.1-2024 audit while
leaving version 1 stable.  Each case names the requirement it covers and has
one or more acceptable outcomes.  The richer fields provide:

    mode            pipe or PTY execution
    environment     additional environment variables
    stdin           UTF-8 or base64 input bytes
    actions         PTY waits, writes, and signals
    fixtures        files created below a private temporary directory
    expect           acceptable status, output, transcript, and file results
    timeout_ms      optional per-case timeout

The token @TMP@ in UTF-8 strings expands to the temporary directory used for a
case.  Fixture and expected-file paths are relative and cannot escape it.
An expected status can be an exact integer, "nonzero", or "any".  Output can
be compared exactly or checked for required byte strings and a minimum length,
so requirements with implementation-defined diagnostics remain portable.

requirements.json is a paraphrased coverage map for the POSIX ed page.  It
contains requirement identifiers and public test locations, not copied
standard or private-suite assertion text.

Run both corpus versions against tsed:

    bun run test:portable

Run version 2 against another implementation, optionally selecting cases:

    bun test/portable_v2_runner.ts --editor /path/to/ed
    bun test/portable_v2_runner.ts --editor /path/to/ed --case address

Use --json to obtain a machine-readable result report.

Do not edit generated JSON by hand.  Change the compact families in the
generator sources and regenerate every public artifact with:

    bun run generate:portable
